jflint@csws5.ic.sunysb.edu (Jesse Flint) writes:

>In article <1992Apr8.155128.4183@newstand.syr.edu> mitanu@mothra.cns.syr.EDU (M i t a n u  P a u l) writes:
>>Hi netters,
>>
>>Do you know what happens if you kill a shopkeeper? 
>
>Yes -- you're in BIIIIIIG trouble.
 
Not true at all. If you are not chaotic your god will be unimpressed with your
actions, and your alignment gets lowered. Your luck goes down by 2. You may also
lose intrinsic telepathy if you have it. However, these things are of minor
significance. You are only in BIG trouble if you try but DON'T manage to kill
the shopkeeper ;-).

>>I chose the Tourist
>>character and got into an antique shop with Fiddo. I got a couple of identify
>>scrolls from the shop, read them and identified two wands (again from the
>>shop) -- slow monster & wand of fire. I then got a potion which I drank
>>and became invisible.
>>
>
>Shopkeepers don't trust invisible customers -- it's too easy for them to
>shoplift. If you're invisible, they'll stand in the doorway and keep you
>from leaving/entering.
>
>>So I got myself in line with the shopkeeper (he was blocking door)
>>and zapped the wand of slow monster. "<shopkeeper's name> is angry"
>>appeared, but nothing else. Then I zapped the wand of fire three/four times
>>towards the shopkeeper. Nothing happened except that he got angry
>>and on the final zap was killed. I got about $2000 gold and saw
>>quite a few monsters converging on me.
>>
>Slow Monster is probably the only reason you survived... 
 
Not true either. If you are invisible, the shopkeeper won't leave the doorway
and you can blast away with wands in complete safety. Slow monster made no
difference.

>>
>>I managed to get me and Fido into the next level and found myself into
>>a shop where the shopkeeper was invisible! Did anyone encounter this
>>before?
>>Also, is it true that it is bad luck to kill a shopkeeper?

>Yeah,  just SLIGHTLY bad luck... Killing a shopkeeper causes you to have
>intrinsic "Aggravate Monsters", which not only get monsters after you but
>will annoy other shopkeepers (yes, they're monsters too...) Shopkeepers are
>also tough -- one I encountered as a 1st level character had AC0 and 11 hit
>dice... not exactly an easy kill. Better just to train yer pet to steal for
>you.

This is garbage as well. Killing a shopkeeper does NOT give you "Aggravate
Monster" intrinsic. If for some reason you might want that you should eat his
corpse. That will give you the intrinsic, the same as eating any human corpse.
Also, having aggravate monster does NOT annoy other shopkeepers.
Also, having aggravate monster is NOT a huge disaster anyway. About all it
does is wake sleeping monsters, and if you don't eat cats, dogs or humans you
won't ever get it.

